wireless: makefile: gate aic8800 by AIC_WLAN_SUPPORT

The aic8800_sdio directory is gated in drivers/net/wireless/Makefile by
CONFIG_SPARD_WLAN_SUPPORT, but that symbol has no Kconfig definition
anywhere (olddefconfig strips any hand-written entry), so the directory
is never built even with AIC_WLAN_SUPPORT=y (which is why the vendor
could only ship out-of-tree .ko files).
Gate it by the really existing CONFIG_AIC_WLAN_SUPPORT instead; the
sub-Makefile forces :=m, so all three drivers (aic8800_bsp/fdrv/btlpm)
are built as loadable modules.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/Makefile
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 #

 obj-$(CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_ADMTEK) += admtek/
-obj-$(CONFIG_SPARD_WLAN_SUPPORT) += aic8800_sdio/
+obj-$(CONFIG_AIC_WLAN_SUPPORT) += aic8800_sdio/
 obj-$(CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_ATH) += ath/
 obj-$(CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_ATMEL) += atmel/
 obj-$(CONFIG_WLAN_VENDOR_BROADCOM) += broadcom/
